# Rust workspace artifacts
target/
**/*.rs.bk
# PyO3 extension modules built into per-crate python-source dirs by
# `maturin develop`. Source of truth is the Rust code; the .so is a build
# artifact.
crates/**/python/**/*.so
crates/**/python/**/*.abi3.so
crates/**/python/**/*.pyd
# model weights / large artifacts — never commit
weights/
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.bin
# local runtime
.cache/
*.log
benchmark-results/

# CPU AMX kernel build artifacts
kernels/cpu/*/build/
kernels/cpu/*/*.so

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store

# uv lockfile — repo flow is `uv venv` / `uv pip install`, not `uv sync`
uv.lock

# repercep.ai marketing site — NOT Repercep source. Canonical location is the
# separate PUBLIC repo github.com/miteshs/repercep-site (~/Projects/repercep-site),
# published to https://repercep.ai via GitHub Pages. Edit there, never here.
#
# A local site/ directory is therefore an untracked MIRROR that goes stale
# silently. On 2026-08-16 a project audit read this stale copy, found the
# pre-pivot "compute substrate for world models" framing plus the dropped
# Repercep Worlds product, and concluded the public site contradicted the pivot
# strategy — which was WRONG; the live site had been correct for weeks.
#
# Also: this repo is PRIVATE and holds confidential strategy/pricing/partner
# material. Never copy content from here into a repercep-site path, including
# an unreferenced file — GitHub Pages still serves it.
site/
*.pdf

